&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a MarTech Developer, you&#39;ll be tasked with working on a variety of client-facing marketing technology initiatives. Working within cross-functional project teams, your responsibilities will include designing, implementing, and optimizing marketing technology solutions that help organizations better engage customers, improve marketing performance, and unlock valuable business insights. This role is ideal for technically-minded developers who enjoy solving complex business challenges and want to work at the intersection of software development, data, and digital marketing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, develop, and maintain custom integrations between CRM, marketing automation, analytics, and other business platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build scalable solutions that support lead generation, customer engagement, personalization, and marketing measurement initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop custom applications, APIs, workflows, and automation solutions to support client marketing and business objectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement and configure marketing technology platforms such as Adobe Experience Platform (AEP), Real-Time CDP (RT-CDP), Adobe Journey Optimizer (AJO), Customer Journey Analytics (CJA), Adobe Analytics, Adobe Campaign, Adobe Workfront, or others&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with strategists, designers, developers, and client stakeholders to translate business requirements into technical solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with data sources, APIs, and reporting platforms to enable actionable insights and improve decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in code reviews and testing processes to ensure high-quality, maintainable software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research emerging technologies, platforms, and best practices within the MarTech ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate clearly and effectively with project teams and clients throughout the development lifecycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of professional experience in software development, marketing technology, solutions engineering, or a related technical role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong programming skills in one or more modern languages such as JavaScript, TypeScript, Python, Java, or C#&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience and proficiency utilizing Adobe martech platforms such as: Adobe Experience Platform (AEP), Real-Time CDP (RT-CDP), Adobe Journey Optimizer (AJO), Customer Journey Analytics (CJA), Adobe Analytics, Adobe Campaign, Adobe Workfront, or others&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with APIs, web services, webhooks, and system integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of modern web technologies, including HTTP, REST APIs, authentication methods, and cloud-based applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity working with non-Adobe marketing automation platforms such as Salesforce Marketing Cloud, HubSpot, Marketo, Pardot, Braze, or similar technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with customer data platforms (CDPs), analytics platforms, and marketing attribution concepts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with relational databases and SQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of data structures, data modeling, and data integration best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent problem-solving and analytical skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and stakeholder management skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive personality and a desire to deliver exceptional client outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for technology and a drive to continuously learn and improve&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Certifications in any related Adobe platforms are an asset.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have you taken any courses at BrainStation? A lot of our design and development best practices and processes are taught during our courses - make sure to highlight this experience in your cover letter if you have!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Konrad is committed to maintaining a diverse work environment and is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants, regardless of race, colour, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status will receive consideration for employment. If you have any accessibility requirements or concerns regarding the hiring process or employment with us, please notify us so we can provide suitable accommodation.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The estimated compensation for this position is $90,000 to $120,000.&lt;/strong&gt; This is an estimate and a compensation offer will vary based on applicant’s education, experience, skills, abilities and alignment with market data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While we sincerely appreciate all applications, only those candidates selected for an interview will be contacted.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;
